1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
You

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
You

4
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You

5
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
I'm always searching

6
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,560
I've always been searching.

7
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:33,560
Hmm.

8
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,280
That's unlucky.

9
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,760
I got one with kelp.

10
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:45,880
They're all filled with kelp today.

11
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,540
Huh? Why'd you do that, Akane?

12
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,480
I told you 10,000 times.

13
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,260
Tuna mayo.

14
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,780
I like kelp.

15
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:52,440
That's right.

16
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,100
You lost to Aoi, man.

17
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,460
Yeah, even though you said it 10,000 times.

18
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,520
You shut up.

19
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,320
Come on. Time to practice.

20
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,160
Huh?

21
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,480
Hold on. I'm not done eating yet.

22
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,740
Hurry up and finish.

23
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,260
My Akane special's sounding freaking awesome.

24
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,800
What a dumb name.

25
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:10,580
Huh?

26
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:12,640
Hey, I...

27
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,540
I wanna play.

28
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:15,220
Yeah?

29
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:17,480
Want me to teach you a little guitar?

30
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:20,920
So?

31
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,540
What do you wanna play?

32
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:24,880
Huh?

33
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:25,400
Huh?

34
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,980
Huh? What? For real?

35
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:30,500
Oh, man, that's adorable.

36
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,320
You must really look up to me, huh, kiddo?

37
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:33,580
No!

38
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,200
Not a chance.

39
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:38,240
But girl bass players are pretty cool.

40
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:38,960
For sure.

41
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:40,580
Okay, then, Al.

42
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,420
You're gonna grow up and become our bassist.

43
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:43,840
What?

44
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,240
Hey, what'll happen to me?

45
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,560
Sounds fun, huh, Aoi?

46
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:47,700
I don't know, Abo.

47
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:48,480
You'll sing backup.

48
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,100
What?

49
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:51,220
Or you could be our dancer.

50
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:53,560
Jeez, Pomba, you really...

51
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,180
Stop, stop.

52
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,140
What happened to practicing?

53
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:56,560
What should we play?

54
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,060
Uh...

55
00:02:59,060 --> 00:02:59,560
Hmm.

56
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,180
Akane?

57
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,460
Play the usual.

58
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:03,680
There you go.

59
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:04,820
That one again.

60
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,500
Count us off, Michinko.

61
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:07,940
If you say so.

62
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:09,080
Hey, wait a second.

63
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:10,880
Come on, I said wait!

64
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,800
Pomba, your mic's not plugged in.

65
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:13,420
Really?

66
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:14,900
Okay, are we ready?

67
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,880
If you can get there...

68
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,880
If you can get there...

69
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:34,880
If you can get there...

70
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:53,340
But...

71
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:56,340
Sometimes...

72
00:03:56,340 --> 00:04:01,980
Just seems too far away.

73
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:04,060
A terrible accident.

74
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,680
They were both in the car.

75
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,860
I heard the other driver was distracted.

76
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,540
Two toddlers left to fend for themselves.

77
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,900
It's just so horrible.

78
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,180
Akane's a senior in high school, right?

79
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,980
What'll they do?

80
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,960
Little one, be sure to listen to your sister, okay?

81
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:24,600
You girls will have to really work together from now on.

82
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:39,980
I don't think I can go.

83
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:43,880
Why?

84
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,040
What do you mean?

85
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,400
We're not moving to Tokyo together?

86
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:52,640
Akane!

87
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:57,960
Hey, stop bullying Akane, butthead!

88
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,420
Awe!

89
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,700
Don't take her away!

90
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,340
Me be fatty!

91
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,000
Fatty?

92
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:05,180
My body fat's only 7%, you know.

93
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:06,420
Shut up, Fatty!

94
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,120
Stinky gorilla!

95
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,620
You can't take Akane away!

96
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:13,000
Akane stays with me!

97
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:24,960
So I'm still searching.

98
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,040
So I'm still searching.

99
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,940
You can't take it.

100
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,000
Wooohoo!

101
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:53,840
Wooohoo!

102
00:05:53,840 --> 00:06:00,840
Wooohoo!

103
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,380
Woooo!

104
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:07,900
Woohoo!

105
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:09,960
Wooo!

106
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:36,920
I'm searching for that place where all my dreams will come true.

107
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:46,960
Hey, what's up?

108
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,960
I'm moving to Tokyo.

109
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,960
I certainly see the appeal.

110
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,960
But this wouldn't be for university, right?

111
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,960
You'll be working?

112
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:57,960
Well, yeah.

113
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,960
At least until my band hits the big time.

114
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:00,960
Your band, huh?

115
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:01,960
How many members?

116
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,960
What members?

117
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:03,960
It's only me.

118
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,960
Sounds like you'll be keeping that day job.

119
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,960
Okay, next.

120
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:08,960
Otaki, come on in.

121
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:12,960
Yes, sir.

122
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,960
Oh, she's the coolest.

123
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:15,960
Otaki, hurry up.

124
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,960
So, my career plan is I'm gonna get married.

125
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:18,960
Woo!

126
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,960
I haven't exactly found Mr. Hart yet, but...

127
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,960
Alright, so you'll be working.

128
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:22,960
Got it.

129
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,960
Okay, next.

130
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,960
I wanted to talk about my plan.

131
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,960
Thank you, my boy.

132
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:36,960
We're starting to prepare for the end of year festival, so City Hall's getting pretty busy.

133
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,960
I might not be able to pick you up next month.

134
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:39,960
Ugh.

135
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:43,960
You expect me to waste an hour of my life walking to and from school every day?

136
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,960
Well, it's the right season for it.

137
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,960
It's nice to walk through the mountains and see the leaves change.

138
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:49,960
Ugh.

139
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,960
I really hate the mountains.

140
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:53,960
Oh?

141
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:58,960
Living in a mountain valley basically just means you're walled in.

142
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,960
It's like we're prisoners being held in a giant jail.

143
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:03,960
My gosh.

144
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,960
Here we go again with the teen angst.

145
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,960
Whatever you want to call it.

146
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:10,960
Doesn't matter because I'm getting the heck out of this town.

147
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:25,960
Hang on.

148
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:30,960
Good afternoon.

149
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:31,960
Hello.

150
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,960
Lovely to see you, Akane.

151
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,960
Aoi.

152
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:35,960
Welcome back.

153
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,960
What are you up to?

154
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,960
Oh, well, Masamichi invited too many people for tonight's assembly.

155
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:43,960
So we ended up borrowing some seat cushions and tables from Yamaguchi.

156
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:44,960
Oh, let me help you with that.

157
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,960
There's no need to put yourself out.

158
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:47,960
Come help, Aoi.

159
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,960
We don't want to hold you up on your way home.

160
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,960
Not at all.

161
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,960
I'm also going to the assembly.

162
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:56,960
Oh, right.

163
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,960
Hey, want some of these pairs?

164
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,960
Really?

165
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,960
I'd love some.

166
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,960
Thank you so much.

167
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:02,960
You've got such a sweet big sister.

168
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,960
You should be grateful for her, Aoi.

169
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,960
Being told to be grateful all the time...

170
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,960
It just makes me want to rebel even more.

171
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,960
No, listen to me.

172
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:18,960
A miso potato stall really needs to have a variety of flavor options.

173
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:22,960
We could add yuzu or chili pepper to the miso.

174
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,960
You think something like this will actually draw a crowd?

175
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,960
Hey, have a little more faith in this, buddy.

176
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:32,960
There are so many nice tourist spots around here, but people always stay in the city.

177
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:36,960
We need something big if we want to break through and attract attention.

178
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:37,960
Exactly.

179
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,960
We should try and ride this way.

180
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,960
Masamichi from the tourism division did us a favor.

181
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,960
Yeah.

182
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:43,960
And we don't want to waste the opportunity.

183
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:44,960
Yeah.

184
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:49,960
You know, over at city hall, there's a rumor that he moved around a lot of money for this.

185
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,960
Stop spreading lies, Akane!

186
00:09:50,960 --> 00:10:03,960
You gonna perform, Aoi?

187
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:10,960
The moment my music starts being used to revitalize the town is when it stops being music.

188
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:15,960
Instead of something enjoyable, it'll become the acoustic representation of my suffering.

189
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:21,960
I'm sure you think you said something super deep and profound just now, but I promise you didn't.

190
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:27,960
But anyway, the music's gonna bring people in and transform this town.

191
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,960
Aoi! Tsugu!

192
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,960
Hm? Dad?

193
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:42,960
Uh, so are you gonna be rocking out over at the shrine hall tonight?

194
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,960
Yeah.

195
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,960
Wrap it up before nine, okay?

196
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:48,960
Hearing bass music on the wind gives me the heebie-jeebies that late at night.

197
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,960
You know, there's a soundproof room in our house.

198
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:55,960
What?

199
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,960
Haven't you ever wanted a big brother?

200
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,960
What?

201
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,960
Dad, please, at least try to play it cool.

202
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,960
I'm not gonna set my sister up with a divorcee.

203
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:09,960
Hey, now! I was the one who got cheated on! I'm an honest and faithful divorcee!

204
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,960
Who cares?

205
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:11,960
Hey!

206
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,960
Hey, Aoi!

207
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,960
Yeah?

208
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,960
Do you remember our old buddy Shino?

209
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,960
Uh, kind of? Why?

210
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:24,960
No, nothing. It's totally fine if you don't.

211
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,960
Hmph.

212
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,960
Hmm.

213
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,960
About what my dad said earlier.

214
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:51,960
It's not like I'm taking his side or anything.

215
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,960
But he is actually serious about...

216
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,960
Can you refrain from talking about that in here, please?

217
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,960
So it's okay to talk about it elsewhere?

218
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:00,960
It's not okay.

219
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:05,960
But... better than in here.

220
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:10,960
No, not like that. Look, you gotta press down harder.

221
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:11,960
Mm-hmm.

222
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,960
Oh.

223
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:19,960
Whoa, wow. I just noticed that... you got a birthmark in your eye.

224
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:20,960
Hey, look.

225
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:21,960
Me too.

226
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,960
They say eye birthmarks mean you're destined for stardom.

227
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:27,960
You and I are both eyeball stars.

228
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,960
Oh, eyeball stars!

229
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,960
What kind of name is that? That's so random.

230
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:34,960
I don't know.

231
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,960
It's not funny. Cut it out. It's a cool name.

232
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:37,960
Cool luck name!

233
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:52,960
Whoa! Wasn't Donkichi Nitobe on the New Year's Eve special a while back?

234
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:57,960
Oh, now I remember him. Didn't he ride on that sparkly portable shrine?

235
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,960
Yeah! I do remember seeing that.

236
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:04,960
We've asked him to compose a song for our town and perform it at the festival.

237
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:09,960
What if he writes about fireworks exploding and then we could, like, set some off?

238
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:12,960
Fireworks? Awesome.

239
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,960
Guess you moved some serious money around after all, huh?

240
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,960
Listen. The stakes are high here.

241
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,960
Because, well, I... see, my own life happens to be on the line.

242
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,960
So I'm really counting on your help with this event, Hakane.

243
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,960
Huh?

244
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:32,960
I've already arranged it with the Citizens Affairs Division.

245
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:34,960
I heard about that. Break a leg.

246
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:35,960
I'm sure it'll be great.

247
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,960
Wait, what?

248
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:38,960
We're about to get started.

249
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,960
All right, then. We'll hash out the details later.

250
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:43,960
Wait, Michinko!

251
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,960
Well, looks like our department does have some pull.

252
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:47,960
Good luck with that.

253
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:57,960
Michinko has a giant crush on you. You know that, right?

254
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,960
Mm-hmm. I've noticed.

255
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:03,960
Great, so don't do anything that might give him false hope.

256
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:12,960
He's my childhood friend. And now my coworker.

257
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,960
With relationships, sometimes you have to leave things alone, even if they're really obvious.

258
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,960
That's the adult way to handle it.

259
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,960
Gosh, adults are so boring.

260
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,960
More importantly...

261
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,960
Hm?

262
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,960
Have you maybe given it some more thought?

263
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:32,960
What?

264
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:33,960
Going to college.

265
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,960
It's not like you can't play in a band and be a student.

266
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,960
Stop. We've gone over this.

267
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,960
You promised you wouldn't bring it up anymore.

268
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:44,960
Hm.

269
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:45,960
So cut it out.

270
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:47,960
Don't break your promise.

271
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,960
Well, I'm off to practice.

272
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:54,960
Okay.

273
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,960
So...

274
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,960
What?

275
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,960
Mm-hm.

276
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:29,960
You go.

277
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:59,940
We'll be right back.

278
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,080
No, stop!

279
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:03,220
What the heck is the matter with you?

280
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:04,900
You've got zero sense of rhythm.

281
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:05,880
You're way off beat.

282
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:06,740
Huh?

283
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,360
Hmm?

284
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,040
Who are you?

285
00:16:15,940 --> 00:16:16,540
What?

286
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,040
Hey.

287
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,240
You and I are eyeball stars.

288
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,380
Shin-no?

289
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:25,140
Hmm?

290
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:27,340
How do you know...

291
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:29,000
Wait, that's the school's uniform.

292
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,240
Hey, are you one of my fans?

293
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:33,760
Want to shake hands?

294
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:35,960
So...

295
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,840
What?

296
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:41,680
Hmm.

297
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,420
You really are, Shin-no?

298
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,500
Yeah, that's what I'm telling you.

299
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:49,080
And you are...

300
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:51,680
Hey, stop!

301
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,200
Wait up!

302
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:54,540
Hang on a minute!

303
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,020
Hey!

304
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,740
What the hell is going on?

305
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,400
Hey!

306
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,260
Let me out of here!

307
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:18,260
Ah, Akane!

308
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:20,120
You're back?

309
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:21,260
Already done with practice?

310
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,040
I'm making your favorite tonight.

311
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,220
Ground meat cutlets.

312
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:25,260
Shin-no just...

313
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:28,440
Sorry.

314
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:28,520
Sorry.

315
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,440
Tell me...

316
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,600
What happened with Shin-no?

317
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:32,720
Uh...

318
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:35,000
Well, uh...

319
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,820
Right, I just thought of him while I was practicing.

320
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,640
And I was wondering...

321
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:41,460
Um...

322
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,020
What he's up to these days.

323
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,320
We fell out of contact a long time ago.

324
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,580
You know, he...

325
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:51,220
Well, he could be dead for all I know.

326
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:55,380
Oh, yeah.

327
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:56,840
That's a total possibility.

328
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:59,120
The only possibility, right?

329
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,320
I mean...

330
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,660
He looks like he hasn't aged at all.

331
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,160
Are we?

332
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:05,820
Hey!

333
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,700
Looks like you left the front door open!

334
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,520
That's very dangerous.

335
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:10,560
Michinko?

336
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:11,380
Akane!

337
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,400
What are you two still doing here?

338
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:14,260
What does he mean?

339
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:15,140
Wait...

340
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:15,440
Whatever!

341
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:16,500
There's no time!

342
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:17,460
Huh?

343
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:19,300
You gotta help with this thing!

344
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,840
Yeah, we talked about this.

345
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:23,200
Oh, did I forget to tell you about the thing today?

346
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,120
Today?

347
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:24,600
Ah!

348
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:25,520
It doesn't matter!

349
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,320
Just come with me!

350
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:31,760
Right when he steps out, we open it.

351
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,500
And try to look cheerful, okay?

352
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:37,880
Dad, did you really spend all night making this thing?

353
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:38,260
Hey!

354
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:39,740
Don't spill any miso on it!

355
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:40,940
So pointless.

356
00:18:41,180 --> 00:18:42,060
I don't even have time for this stuff.

357
00:18:42,060 --> 00:18:43,360
Wait, why is he coming today?

358
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,440
Isn't the event a week from now?

359
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:57,420
Well, yeah, but Nitobe is legendary for writing songs about specific towns, and he says he needs to try all the local foods and get to know the people to feel the warmth of the town and sing directly to the soul of the area.

360
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,560
And City Hall is gonna pay for all that?

361
00:18:59,720 --> 00:18:59,900
Yeah!

362
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:03,580
So this guy's basically a freeloader.

363
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:06,220
Sugu?

364
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:19,400
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you so very much for waiting.

365
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:22,820
The one and only Dunkin' Itobe has arrived.

366
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,900
I've come from far, far away.

367
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:29,500
I've crossed plains and mountains just for the pleasure of putting a smile on all of your faces.

368
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:30,140
What?

369
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:30,460
No.

370
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:31,220
Oh, Dunkin' Itobe!

371
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,120
What's so true?

372
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:33,180
Really?

373
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:33,660
No.

374
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:33,800
No.

375
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,800
Hmm?

376
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,800
Hmm?

377
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,800
Makanu?

378
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:50,800
Uh...

379
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,800
Shin-Pet...

380
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,800
Shin-No...

381
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:55,800
Come on, Tsugu!

382
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,800
Hold it the right way!

383
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,800
What?

384
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,800
Oh, wait!

385
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:24,800
Gah...

386
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,800
Mom...

387
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:33,800
Dad...

388
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:35,800
...and all of my ancestors...

389
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,800
...hunt me your strength!

390
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,800
Oh, hey...

391
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:43,800
...I got a receipt, so do you...

392
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,800
...huh?

393
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,800
Wait...

394
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:49,800
...so was that...

395
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,800
...Shino guy really there after all?

396
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:53,800
Yeah...

397
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,800
...I was sure he was a ghost...

398
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,800
...but then...

399
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,800
...we saw the real Shin-No at the station...

400
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,800
...so the one I saw earlier...

401
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:01,800
...Doppelganger?

402
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:02,800
I don't know!

403
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,800
But I'm sure that was Shin-No too!

404
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,800
I don't get it, but there's definitely something weird going on!

405
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:12,800
See anything?

406
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:13,800
Hmm...

407
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:15,800
There's no one in here...

408
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:16,800
Huh?

409
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:18,800
That can't be true...

410
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,800
Hey, what gives?

411
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:22,800
Huh...

412
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,800
...you ran scared!

413
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:24,800
Yeah!

414
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:26,800
Hey, you let her go!

415
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:29,800
Huh?

416
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:30,800
Huh?

417
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:31,800
What's this kid?

418
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:32,800
Looks just like Machinko!

419
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,800
Tell us who you are right now!

420
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:38,800
I already told you who I am!

421
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:39,800
I'm Shino!

422
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:40,800
Who the heck are you?

423
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,800
It's time to run, Ao!

424
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,800
What?

425
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,800
Okay?

426
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:44,800
Did you...

427
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:45,800
...say Ao?

428
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:47,800
I'm Aoi...

429
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,800
Aoi...

430
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:49,800
...Aoi...

431
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:50,800
...Aibo Star...

432
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:51,800
...Number Two!

433
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:54,800
Huh?

434
00:21:58,800 --> 00:21:59,800
That day...

435
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:02,800
...when Akane told me she wasn't coming to Tokyo...

436
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:07,800
...I just couldn't make myself leave...

437
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:09,800
...So I stayed in here...

438
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:10,800
...thinking things over...

439
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:11,800
...and...

440
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:12,800
...before I knew it...

441
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:13,800
...uh...

442
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:14,800
...it was the morning?

443
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,800
Why is that a question?

444
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:16,800
Well, I don't get it either!

445
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,800
I just started to nod off...

446
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:18,800
...so I laid down right there...

447
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:19,800
...and then this awful noise woke me up!

448
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:20,800
Awful?!

449
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:31,800
...

450
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:34,800
...It didn't really seem like anything happened...

451
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:37,800
...but here you are telling me it's been 13 years...

452
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,800
...it doesn't feel real...

453
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:40,800
Oh yeah...

454
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,800
...just like Rip Van Winkle...

455
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:43,800
...So wait...

456
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:44,800
...does that mean...

457
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,800
Anyway...

458
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:49,800
...there's no use sitting around crying over all the time I've lost...

459
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:51,800
How are you accepting this so fast?

460
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:52,800
I mean...

461
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,800
...it's all thanks to you guys...

462
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:56,800
...you two make coping easy...

463
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,800
...man, you really are a mini version of Machinko, huh?

464
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:00,800
Read the room...

465
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:01,800
Whatever he is...

466
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,800
...I'm sure it isn't a ghost...

467
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:04,800
...his body's tangible...

468
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,800
Uh...

469
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:06,800
...okay...

470
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:07,800
...but then...

471
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:08,800
...hmm...

472
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:11,800
...a living spirit?

473
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:12,800
A living spirit?

474
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:13,800
A living spirit?

475
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:14,800
People...

476
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:15,800
...have told tales...

477
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,800
...about how if you have strong feelings for someone...

478
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:21,800
...you can unconsciously send a living spirit of yourself to be with them...

479
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:22,800
I've heard of that...

480
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,800
...some people do that to curse or kill someone...

481
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:25,800
...oh...

482
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,800
...and, uh...

483
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,800
...Shino did get dumped by Akane...

484
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:31,800
...maybe this spirit was created out of that regret...

485
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,800
...what are you saying?

486
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,800
Huh?

487
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:35,800
I have no regrets...

488
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:38,800
...because I haven't given up on anything yet...

489
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,800
...what?

490
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,800
I've thought it over and made my decision...

491
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:43,800
...I'm gonna move to Tokyo...

492
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,800
...I'm gonna become a big-time musician...

493
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:46,800
...and then...

494
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,800
...I'll make a glorious return to be with Akane!

495
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:50,800
What's with the crazy optimism?

496
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:51,800
Oh no!

497
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,800
Why do bad things always happen to good people?

498
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:54,800
Akane...

499
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:56,800
...must be 31 now...

500
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:57,800
...so...

501
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:58,800
...31 and...

502
00:23:58,800 --> 00:23:59,800
...30...

503
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:00,800
...uh...

504
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:01,800
...wait...

505
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:02,800
...Akane isn't married, right?

506
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:03,800
Right.

507
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:04,800
Awesome!

508
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:05,800
I mean...

509
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:06,800
...I guess I shouldn't be happy about that...

510
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,800
...doesn't matter...

511
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:08,800
...hurry up and marry her.

512
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:09,800
You wanna...

513
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:10,800
...meet her?

514
00:24:10,800 --> 00:24:11,800
You idiot!

515
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:12,800
I can't meet her yet!

516
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:13,800
You're an idiot!

517
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,800
Have you not been listening this whole time?

518
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:17,800
I need to become a big-time musician first!

519
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,800
I don't know if I'd say big-time, but...

520
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:20,800
...he's in a band, right?

521
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,800
Huh?

522
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:22,800
Oh...

523
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:23,800
...yeah, I guess so.

524
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:25,800
Your 31-year-old self...

525
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,800
...is actually a musician.

526
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,800
Huh.

527
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,800
I'M SO COOL!

528
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:33,800
Okay...

529
00:24:33,800 --> 00:24:34,800
...I'm heading out.

530
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:35,800
See ya!

531
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:36,800
Wait!

532
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:41,800
Huh?

533
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:42,800
Huh?

534
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,800
So, this sure is some turn of fate, huh?

535
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:48,800
For sure!

536
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:50,800
I knew that if someone was gonna write a song for our town...

537
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:51,800
...it had to be you.

538
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:56,800
And then coincidence struck as I just happened to be looking through your concert videos...

539
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,800
...and I saw my old friend in your backup band!

540
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:00,800
Hey, Shino!

541
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:01,800
That hurt.

542
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:05,800
This performance will be Shinosuke's triumphant homecoming.

543
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:08,800
We should be sure to feature his guitar solo.

544
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:09,800
Oh, sweet!

545
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:11,800
Can there be a saxophone solo, too?

546
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:14,800
Yeah, your sax doesn't really have that punch we need.

547
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:15,800
You know what I mean?

548
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:17,800
Hey, what do you mean by punch?

549
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:20,800
So, did you tell Aoi that Shino was coming home?

550
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:21,800
Hmm?

551
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,800
Did you just say something, Akane?

552
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:25,800
Hey, hey, hey!

553
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:28,800
Is something going on between you two?

554
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:29,800
Huh?

555
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:32,800
How about we just leave that to the imagination, okay?

556
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:33,800
Stop, Michinko!

557
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:34,800
What did I say?

558
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:35,800
Ugh!

559
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:36,800
The beer's already gone flat.

560
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:37,800
Can I get the high-end stuff?

561
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:38,800
Oh!

562
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:39,800
And more meat, please.

563
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,800
Hmm...

564
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,800
Maybe...

565
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:45,800
...he's a ghost tied to the shrine hall?

566
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:48,800
Yeah, like he knows he's trapped but still tries to leave.

567
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,800
Your wildest dreams will come true.

568
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:56,800
Back then, I really believed it.

